{
    "version":  "0.3.12",
    "notes":  [
                  {
                      "version":  "0.3.12",
                      "text":  "### Changed\n- **Automatic Game Capture is now OBS\u0027s own method**: Crossfeed just sets your Game Capture sources to \"Capture any fullscreen application\", with the game\u0027s audio. It never reads or touches your games, so it is safe with anti-cheat (BattlEye, EAC).\n\n### Fixed\n- **Replay buffer notifications are only for you**: the banner no longer shows up in your stream, in recordings or in saved clips. It stays visible on your screen (Windows 10 version 2004 or later).\n- **Chat comes back after you restart your LIVE**: TikTok chat, joins, gifts and follows now reconnect within seconds when you end the LIVE and start it again. Twitch chat and events also reconnect on their own after a network drop or sleep."
                  },
                  {
                      "version":  "0.3.11",
                      "text":  "### New\n- **Replay buffer notifications**: a small banner in the top-right corner of the screen, like ShadowPlay\u0027s, when the replay buffer starts, saves a replay or stops. It never takes the focus from your game and clicks go through it. Turn it off from Crossfeed → Replay Buffer Notifications, or in the Setup Wizard, which shows all three banners.\n\n### Fixed\n- The **Setup Wizard** moves on as soon as you press Next after entering a channel: saving and reconnecting the chats now happens in the background."
                  },
                  {
                      "version":  "0.3.10",
                      "text":  "### New\n- **Update notices**: when OBS starts, Crossfeed tells you when a new version is ready, with a button to restart OBS right away. The notice never takes the keyboard, so typing in the chat can\u0027t close it or restart OBS.\n- **Latest** or **New update** next to Crossfeed → Check for Updates, so you always know where you are.\n- **What\u0027s New**: after an update, a window shows what changed. Open it again any time from Crossfeed → What\u0027s New.\n- Crossfeed checks for updates every time OBS starts, instead of once a day."
                  },
                  {
                      "version":  "0.3.9",
                      "text":  "### New\n- **Twitch\u0027s highlights at the top of the chat**: gift banners, polls, predictions, the Hype Train and pinned messages, like Twitch\u0027s own chat.\n- The Twitch and TikTok icons in front of the names look like Twitch\u0027s badges.\n\n### Fixed\n- **A new version never stops the one you are running**: updates switch when OBS restarts, pages and plugin together.\n- Follows, channel point rewards, AutoMod and the users in chat keep working when a new version needs a Twitch permission you have not given yet. Reconnect only adds what is missing.\n- /demo shows who received the gifted subs, one line each."
                  },
                  {
                      "version":  "0.3.7",
                      "text":  "### New\n- **The chat looks like Twitch\u0027s own chat**: fonts, spacing, badges, cards, replies and deleted messages.\n- **Moderator icons on hover** (Ban, Timeout, Warn, Delete), in a bar that opens just outside the message.\n- **Chat Style: Multistream**, a compact dark chat with live viewer counters per platform.\n\n### Fixed\n- Chat Size other than 100% no longer misplaces the moderator bar.\n- The Activity dock works on OBS 30.\n- /demo never sends anything to Twitch."
                  }
              ],
